 "files": [
  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Pixelate Region\n\nCovers chosen rectangles of a scene with an opaque mosaic and leaves the rest perfectly sharp, the way a demo hides keys, tokens and addresses. Runs its WebGL shader over its own built-in scene (a credentials page; title, rows and note from variables, with the values of the chosen rows covered), not over the host video.\n\nCategory: filters. Length: 3.0 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A product demo shows real data (API keys, tokens, email addresses, account numbers) that must not leave the building.\n- The reveal is the point: something is deliberately hidden and the viewer should see that it was hidden.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The whole frame wants a treatment rather than a covered rectangle: vhs-filter and crt-screen work edge to edge.\n- What you are covering moves around the frame: a region is a fixed rectangle.\n- You only want to de-emphasise something: a mosaic dense enough to redact is not a soft focus.\n\nVariables:\n- title (string): Title, default \"Project credentials\"\n- rows (string): Rows, default \"Account | casey@example.com; API key | sk_live_4f8a2c9e1b7d; Webhook secret | whsec_71c0d4e8ab35\"\n- note (string): Note, default \"Rotate keys from the dashboard \\u2014 old ones stay valid for 24 hours.\"\n- redact (string): Covered rows, default \"2,3\"\n- cell_size (number, 6-72): Cell size, default 24\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Pixelate Region\n\n  Rectangles of a scene covered with an opaque mosaic, the rest left untouched. The scene\n  here is a settings page whose key rows are covered.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/pixelate-region/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n\n  remocn captures its React children with the HTML-in-Canvas API, which a render machine does\n  not have. This block draws remocn's preview scene (a settings page) (text and colours from the variables) on a\n  2D canvas and runs remocn's fragment shader over it, so it applies the look to its own content,\n  not to the host video behind it.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"pixelate-region\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[{\"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title\", \"description\": \"Heading of the sample settings page.\", \"default\": \"Project credentials\"}, {\"id\": \"rows\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Rows\", \"description\": \"Rows as label | value, separated by semicolons (up to 5).\", \"default\": \"Account | casey@example.com; API key | sk_live_4f8a2c9e1b7d; Webhook secret | whsec_71c0d4e8ab35\"}, {\"id\": \"note\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Note\", \"description\": \"Footnote under the rows.\", \"default\": \"Rotate keys from the dashboard — old ones stay valid for 24 hours.\"}, {\"id\": \"redact\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Covered rows\", \"description\": \"Numbers of the rows whose value is covered, separated by commas.\", \"default\": \"2,3\"}, {\"id\": \"cell_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Cell size\", \"description\": \"Size of one mosaic cell. Pixel sizes are for a 1280×720 frame and scale with the frame.\", \"default\": 24, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 72, \"step\": 2, \"unit\": \"px\"}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"quality\", \"label\": \"Resolution\", \"description\": \"Share of the frame size the shader is drawn at, then scaled up. Mosaic cells are large; 0.75 keeps the sharp text around them crisp.\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05}]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Pixelate Region</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600&amp;family=Geist+Mono:wght@400&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          background: #000;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .pxr-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n        }\n        .pxr-canvas,\n        .pxr-scene {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          width: 100%;\n          height: 100%;\n          display: block;\n        }\n        .pxr-scene {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .pxr-off .pxr-canvas {\n          display: none;\n        }\n        .pxr-off .pxr-fb {\n          display: block;\n        }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"pixelate-region\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"pxr-clip\" class=\"pxr-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <canvas id=\"pxr-scene0\" class=\"pxr-scene pxr-fb\"></canvas>\n          <canvas id=\"pxr-canvas\" class=\"pxr-canvas\"></canvas>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var NAME = \"pixelate-region\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var stage = document.getElementById(\"pxr-clip\");\n            var canvas = document.getElementById(\"pxr-canvas\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function clampNum(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function hex(value, fallback) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(String(value || \"\").trim());\n              if (!m) return fallback;\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return \"#\" + h.toLowerCase();\n            }\n            function rgb(value) {\n              var h = hex(value, \"#ffffff\").slice(1);\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) / 255, parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) / 255];\n            }\n            var DEFS = [{\"id\": \"title\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Project credentials\"}, {\"id\": \"rows\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Account | casey@example.com; API key | sk_live_4f8a2c9e1b7d; Webhook secret | whsec_71c0d4e8ab35\"}, {\"id\": \"note\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"Rotate keys from the dashboard — old ones stay valid for 24 hours.\"}, {\"id\": \"redact\", \"type\": \"string\", \"default\": \"2,3\"}, {\"id\": \"cell_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 24, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 72}, {\"id\": \"resolution\", \"type\": \"number\", \"default\": 0.75, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 1}];\n            var V = {};\n            DEFS.forEach(function (d) {\n              var raw = vars[d.id];\n              if (d.type === \"number\") V[d.id] = clampNum(raw, d.default, d.min, d.max);\n              else if (d.type === \"color\") V[d.id] = hex(raw, d.default);\n              else if (d.type === \"boolean\") V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"boolean\" ? raw : raw === \"true\" ? true : raw === \"false\" ? false : d.default;\n              else if (d.type === \"enum\") V[d.id] = d.options.indexOf(raw) >= 0 ? raw : d.default;\n              else V[d.id] = typeof raw === \"string\" && raw.trim() ? raw.trim() : d.default;\n            });\n\n            var W = Math.max(2, root.clientWidth);\n            var H = Math.max(2, root.clientHeight);\n            var res = V.resolution;\n            var cw = Math.max(2, Math.round(W * res));\n            var ch = Math.max(2, Math.round(H * res));\n            var sceneCanvases = [\"pxr-scene0\"].map(function (id) {\n              var el = document.getElementById(id);\n              el.width = cw;\n              el.height = ch;\n              return el;\n            });\n\n            var SANS = \"Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif\";\n            var MONO = \"'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace\";\n            var INK = \"#f2f2f2\";\n            var MUTED = \"#8b8f9a\";\n            var TONES = [\"#a1eebd\", \"#ffb38e\", \"#d4b3ff\"];\n            var S = Math.min(W / 940, H / 720);\n            function setFont(ctx, weight, size, family) { ctx.font = weight + \" \" + size + \"px \" + family; }\n            function fitFont(ctx, text, maxWidth, weight, size, family) {\n              setFont(ctx, weight, size, family);\n              var w = ctx.measureText(text).width;\n              if (w > maxWidth) { size *= maxWidth / w; setFont(ctx, weight, size, family); }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function setSpacing(ctx, px) { if (\"letterSpacing\" in ctx) ctx.letterSpacing = px + \"px\"; }\n            function wrapLines(ctx, text, maxWidth) {\n              var words = String(text).split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n              var lines = [];\n              var line = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (word) {\n                var next = line ? line + \" \" + word : word;\n                if (line && ctx.measureText(next).width > maxWidth) { lines.push(line); line = word; }\n                else line = next;\n              });\n              if (line) lines.push(line);\n              return lines;\n            }\n            function pairs(text, max) {\n              return String(text).split(\";\")\n                .map(function (row) { return row.split(\"|\").map(function (part) { return part.trim(); }); })\n                .filter(function (row) { return row[0]; })\n                .slice(0, max);\n            }\n            function begin(ctx, cw, ch, fill) {\n              ctx.setTransform(cw / W, 0, 0, ch / H, 0, 0);\n              ctx.fillStyle = fill;\n              ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n              ctx.textBaseline = \"middle\";\n              ctx.textAlign = \"left\";\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n            }\n\n\n            // Sample scene \"secrets\": a settings page with credentials (remocn's CanvasSceneSecrets).\n            // drawSecrets returns the rectangle of every value (frame pixels) so a filter can cover them.\n            var secretRows = pairs(V.rows, 5);\n            var secretRects = [];\n            function drawSecrets(canvas) {\n              var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n              begin(ctx, canvas.width, canvas.height, \"#0d0f14\");\n              secretRects = [];\n              var portrait = W < H;\n              var n = secretRows.length;\n              var s, ox = 0, oy = 0, titleY, rowY, pitch, valueX, valueW, noteY, noteMaxW;\n              if (!portrait) {\n                s = Math.min(W / 1280, H / 720);\n                ox = (W - 1280 * s) / 2; oy = (H - 720 * s) / 2;\n                titleY = 104; rowY = 220; pitch = 112; valueX = 504; valueW = 600; \n                noteY = rowY + n * pitch + 12; noteMaxW = 1088;\n              } else {\n                s = W / 760;\n                var content = 104 + n * 168 + 12 + 28 + 70;\n                ox = 0; oy = (H - content * s) / 2;\n                titleY = 0; rowY = 104; pitch = 168; valueX = 64; valueW = 632; \n                noteY = rowY + n * pitch + 12; noteMaxW = 632;\n              }\n              var labelX = portrait ? 64 : 96;\n              ctx.fillStyle = INK;\n              setFont(ctx, 600, 44 * s, SANS);\n              setSpacing(ctx, -0.02 * 44 * s);\n              ctx.fillText(V.title, ox + labelX * s, oy + (titleY + 22) * s);\n              setSpacing(ctx, 0);\n              secretRows.forEach(function (row, i) {\n                var top = rowY + i * pitch;\n                ctx.fillStyle = MUTED;\n                setFont(ctx, 400, 34 * s, SANS);\n                var lx = ox + labelX * s;\n                var ly = oy + (top + 36) * s;\n                if (portrait) { setFont(ctx, 400, 30 * s, SANS); ly = oy + (top - 16) * s; }\n                ctx.fillText(row[0], lx, ly);\n                var vy = top + 36;\n                ctx.fillStyle = INK;\n                fitFont(ctx, row[1] || \"\", (valueW - 8) * s, 400, 34 * s, MONO);\n                ctx.fillText(row[1] || \"\", ox + valueX * s, oy + vy * s);\n                secretRects.push({ x: ox + valueX * s, y: oy + top * s, w: valueW * s, h: 72 * s });\n              });\n              var ny = oy + (noteY + 28) * s;\n              ctx.fillStyle = \"#1e222c\";\n              ctx.fillRect(ox + labelX * s, ny - 28 * s, W - (ox + labelX * s) * 2, Math.max(1, s));\n              ctx.fillStyle = MUTED;\n              setFont(ctx, 400, 28 * s, SANS);\n              wrapLines(ctx, V.note, noteMaxW * s).forEach(function (text, i) {\n                ctx.fillText(text, ox + labelX * s, ny + (i + 0.5) * 28 * s * 1.4);\n              });\n            }\n\n            function drawScenes() {\n              drawSecrets(sceneCanvases[0]);\n            }\n\n            var VERTEX = [\n              \"#version 300 es\",\n              \"in vec2 a_pos;\",\n              \"out vec2 v_uv;\",\n              \"void main() {\",\n              \"  v_uv = vec2(a_pos.x * 0.5 + 0.5, 0.5 - a_pos.y * 0.5);\",\n              \"  gl_Position = vec4(a_pos, 0.0, 1.0);\",\n              \"}\"\n            ].join(\"\\n\");\n            var FRAGMENT = `#version 300 es\nprecision highp float;\n\nuniform sampler2D u_scene;\nuniform vec4 u_regions[8];\nuniform int u_region_count;\nuniform vec2 u_cell;\n\nin vec2 v_uv;\nout vec4 outColor;\n\nconst int TAPS = 3;\n\nvec4 cellAverage(vec2 center, vec2 cell) {\n  vec4 sum = vec4(0.0);\n  for (int y = 0; y < TAPS; y++) {\n    for (int x = 0; x < TAPS; x++) {\n      vec2 offset =\n        (vec2(float(x), float(y)) + 0.5) / float(TAPS) - 0.5;\n      sum += texture(u_scene, center + offset * cell);\n    }\n  }\n  return sum / float(TAPS * TAPS);\n}\n\nvoid main() {\n  vec4 result = texture(u_scene, v_uv);\n  vec2 cell = max(u_cell, vec2(0.0005));\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {\n    if (i >= u_region_count) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    vec4 region = u_regions[i];\n    vec2 lo = region.xy;\n    vec2 hi = region.xy + region.zw;\n    vec2 hit = step(lo, v_uv) * step(v_uv, hi);\n    if (hit.x * hit.y < 0.5) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    vec2 center = lo + (floor((v_uv - lo) / cell) + 0.5) * cell;\n    result = vec4(cellAverage(center, cell).rgb, 1.0);\n  }\n\n  outColor = result;\n}`;\n\n            canvas.width = cw;\n            canvas.height = ch;\n            var gl = canvas.getContext(\"webgl2\", { antialias: false, depth: false, stencil: false, preserveDrawingBuffer: true });\n            function compile(type, source) {\n              var shader = gl.createShader(type);\n              gl.shaderSource(shader, source);\n              gl.compileShader(shader);\n              if (!gl.getShaderParameter(shader, gl.COMPILE_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getShaderInfoLog(shader) || \"shader compile failed\");\n              return shader;\n            }\n            var paint = null;\n            var upload = function () {};\n            var extraUpload = function () {};\n            var frameFn = function () {};\n            var texUnits = [];\n            try {\n              if (!gl) throw new Error(\"WebGL2 is not available\");\n              var program = gl.createProgram();\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.VERTEX_SHADER, VERTEX));\n              gl.attachShader(program, compile(gl.FRAGMENT_SHADER, FRAGMENT));\n              gl.linkProgram(program);\n              if (!gl.getProgramParameter(program, gl.LINK_STATUS)) throw new Error(gl.getProgramInfoLog(program) || \"link failed\");\n              gl.useProgram(program);\n              var buffer = gl.createBuffer();\n              gl.bindBuffer(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, buffer);\n              gl.bufferData(gl.ARRAY_BUFFER, new Float32Array([-1, -1, 1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1]), gl.STATIC_DRAW);\n              var aPos = gl.getAttribLocation(program, \"a_pos\");\n              gl.enableVertexAttribArray(aPos);\n              gl.vertexAttribPointer(aPos, 2, gl.FLOAT, false, 0, 0);\n              function makeTexture(unit) {\n                var texture = gl.createTexture();\n                gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                gl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_S, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_WRAP_T, gl.CLAMP_TO_EDGE);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                gl.texParameteri(gl.TEXTURE_2D, gl.TEXTURE_MAG_FILTER, gl.LINEAR);\n                return texture;\n              }\n              gl.viewport(0, 0, cw, ch);\n              function u(name) { return gl.getUniformLocation(program, name); }\n              [\"u_scene\"].forEach(function (name, unit) {\n                makeTexture(unit);\n                gl.uniform1i(u(name), unit);\n              });\n              gl.uniform1f(u(\"u_aspect\"), W / H);\n              var frameLoc = u(\"u_frame\");\n              var timeLoc = u(\"u_time\");\n              upload = function () {\n                sceneCanvases.forEach(function (el, unit) {\n                  gl.activeTexture(gl.TEXTURE0 + unit);\n                  gl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, el);\n                });\n                extraUpload();\n              };\n\n              var cover = String(V.redact).split(\",\").map(function (n) { return parseInt(n, 10) - 1; }).filter(function (n) { return n >= 0; });\n              gl.uniform2f(u(\"u_cell\"), Math.max(V.cell_size * S, 1) / W, Math.max(V.cell_size * S, 1) / H);\n              var regionsLoc = u(\"u_regions[0]\");\n              var countLoc = u(\"u_region_count\");\n              frameFn = function () {\n                var packed = new Float32Array(32);\n                var count = 0;\n                cover.forEach(function (index) {\n                  var r = secretRects[index];\n                  if (!r || count >= 8) return;\n                  packed[count * 4] = r.x / W;\n                  packed[count * 4 + 1] = r.y / H;\n                  packed[count * 4 + 2] = r.w / W;\n                  packed[count * 4 + 3] = r.h / H;\n                  count++;\n                });\n                gl.uniform4fv(regionsLoc, packed);\n                gl.uniform1i(countLoc, count);\n              };\n\n              paint = function (frame) {\n                gl.uniform1f(frameLoc, frame);\n                gl.uniform1f(timeLoc, frame / 30);\n                frameFn(frame, frame / 30);\n                gl.clearColor(0, 0, 0, 0);\n                gl.clear(gl.COLOR_BUFFER_BIT);\n                gl.drawArrays(gl.TRIANGLE_STRIP, 0, 4);\n              };\n            } catch (err) {\n              stage.classList.add(\"pxr-off\");\n              if (window.console) console.warn(NAME + \":\", err.message);\n            }\n\n            // The scenes are redrawn whenever a web font finishes loading, so no frame keeps a fallback face.\n            var fontEpoch = 0;\n            var sceneEpoch = -1;\n            var lastFrame = 0;\n            function render(frame) {\n              lastFrame = frame;\n              if (sceneEpoch !== fontEpoch) {\n                sceneEpoch = fontEpoch;\n                drawScenes();\n                upload();\n              }\n              if (paint) paint(frame);\n            }\n            if (document.fonts && document.fonts.load) {\n              [\"400 34px Geist\", \"500 30px Geist\", \"600 44px Geist\", \"400 44px 'Geist Mono'\"].forEach(function (face) {\n                document.fonts.load(face).then(function () { fontEpoch++; render(lastFrame); }, function () {});\n              });\n            }\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"3\");\n            var totalFrames = Math.round(total * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(clock, {\n              frame: totalFrames,\n              duration: total,\n              ease: \"none\",\n              onUpdate: function () { render(Math.round(clock.frame)); }\n            }, 0);\n            render(0);\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[NAME] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "6c7dcf8113d2dd113ca9a519f89f267e4a66dc21f90f305a80965414a97efeeb",
